{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MvpmWZAFB2C9oxoGYFZ2WQ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Every tool the scheduling agent may call, with the task it serves.\n# The executor denies any tool not listed here. Annotations from servers (readOnlyHint and so on)\n# are not used for allow or approval decisions.\nrole: scheduling_agent\ntools:\n  - tool: ehr__find_patient\n    reason: Match the sender to a patient record by date of birth and phone or email.\n  - tool: ehr__search_slots\n    reason: List open slots for a provider, location, and visit type.\n  - tool: ehr__get_appointment\n    reason: Read one appointment the patient asks about.\n  - tool: ehr__list_patient_appointments\n    reason: Show the patient their upcoming appointments.\n  - tool: ehr__book_appointment\n    reason: Book a slot the patient chose.\n  - tool: ehr__update_appointment\n    reason: Change time, provider, or status (confirmed / checked_in / no_show / cancelled) of an appointment.\n  - tool: ehr__cancel_appointment\n    reason: Cancel an appointment at the patient's request.\n  - tool: payments__refund_deposit\n    reason: Refund a no-show deposit after staff review.\n  - tool: sms__send_to_patient\n    reason: Send a templated message to the phone number on the patient's record.\n  - tool: sms__send_freeform\n    reason: Send a staff-approved message that is not one of the templates.\n  - tool: insurance__check_eligibility\n    reason: Ask the eligibility agent whether a visit is covered.\nsrc/tools/metadata-scan.ts:56:  { rule: \"url\", re: /\\b(?:https?|ftp|wss?|file|data):\\/?\\/?[^\\s\"'<>]+/i },\nsrc/tools/metadata-scan.ts:113:    // Server-scoped schemes (ehr://...) pass; web, file, and data URLs are findings like anywhere else.\nsrc/tools/registry.ts:12:  url: string;\nsrc/tools/registry.ts:99:   * server's pinned URL and certificate. reportedName is informational only.\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:6:// prompt of that single call in three parts: input_tokens (uncached), cache_read_input_tokens, and\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:7:// cache_creation_input_tokens. Their sum is the full prompt the model read for this decision,\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:8:// including the part served from the prompt cache and the provider's own tool-use preamble, which\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:10:// We record it as \"measured\", with the cached share kept separately.\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:22:  cachedInputTokens: number | null;\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:26:export const USAGE_METHOD = \"anthropic.messages.usage(input+cache_read+cache_creation)\";\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:36:    return { tokens: r.input_tokens, status: \"estimated\", method: COUNT_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: null, compacted: false };\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:38:    return { tokens: null, status: \"unavailable\", method: COUNT_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: null, compacted: false };\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:44:  const cacheRead = usage.cache_read_input_tokens ?? 0;\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:45:  const total = usage.input_tokens + cacheRead + (usage.cache_creation_input_tokens ?? 0);\nsrc/agent/context-size.ts:46:  return { tokens: total, status: \"measured\", method: USAGE_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: cacheRead, compacted: false };\nsrc/agent/budget.ts:61:  cache_read_input_tokens?: number | null;\nsrc/agent/budget.ts:62:  cache_creation_input_tokens?: number | null;\nsrc/agent/budget.ts:122:    const cacheRead = u.cache_read_input_tokens ?? 0;\nsrc/agent/budget.ts:123:    const cacheWrite = u.cache_creation_input_tokens ?? 0;\nsrc/agent/budget.ts:127:        cacheRead * price.cacheRead +\nsrc/agent/budget.ts:128:        cacheWrite * price.cacheWrite) /\nsrc/agent/budget.ts:131:    this.inTok += u.input_tokens + cacheRead + cacheWrite;\nsrc/integrations/sms.ts:31:    const res = await fetch(`${BASE}/messages`, {\nsrc/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:12:// clinic-agent/ehr/<clinicId>; access tokens last 5 minutes and are cached until 30 s before expiry.\nsrc/integratio